ValueFlow v2.0 is out. It is the largest release since the project began, and it concentrates on three things: broader data, smarter attribution, and more control over the analysis surface.

# More platforms

v2.0 adds Lemon Squeezy, Buy Me a Coffee, and Patreon alongside Stripe and Paddle. More important, the data-source plugin interface is now public. Any developer can write an adapter for their own payment provider and ship it without waiting for us.

# Attribution that learns

The old attribution engine was rule-based. The new one adds a lightweight model that estimates the relative contribution of channels and content types to a conversion. It is trained on a public creator-economy dataset, then fine-tuned locally on each deployment, so the result reflects the operator's own audience rather than a generic benchmark.

# Dashboards that fit the business

Drag-and-drop layout, custom metric formulas, and shared team boards bring enterprise BI ergonomics to independent creators. No new pricing tier: the features are in the open-source release.

# Upgrade

The full changelog and migration guide are in the repository. The data model is backward compatible; existing dashboards keep working.
